# From Discord Calls to the Recording Booth: My Voice Acting Ambitions

**Impressions, Creature Sounds, and the Power of Audacity**

If you look at the rest of my portfolio, you will see a lot of structured logic, coding, and design. This section is just pure, unadulterated chaos.

I don't have a professional studio setup, and I don't have a polished demo reel to attach here. What I do have is a very specific, slightly concerning talent for manipulating my voice, and a massive desire to actually put it to use in a real project.

## I. The Origins of the Chaos

This entire pursuit started as a joke. When you spend enough time in discord calls with friends, if you're anything like me, you get bored and start doing bits. Over time, those bits evolved into me genuinely practicing impressions just to get a reaction out of people.

There is a very specific joy in perfectly replicating a character's voice when nobody is expecting it. It went from a stupid party trick to something I genuinely want to explore as a creative medium.

## II. The Repertoire: Monsters and Lemurs

My current roster of impressions is a completely random mixed bag. I can do highly accurate versions of Mort from Madagascar, or something even more niche like Jeff the Landshark from Marvel Rivals. (if you play this game pls hit me up im looking for people to play with)

Beyond specific characters, my real specialty lies in making crazy, niche creature sounds. Because I actively develop indie horror games, I know exactly how much heavy lifting audio does for an immersive atmosphere. I know exactly what kind of weird, guttural, unsettling noises a monster needs to make to actually scare a player, and I know how to produce them myself.

## III. The Natural Vibe: High-Energy Pathos

While deep character impressions are fun, my most natural voice acting style is just... me, dialed up to a hundred.

I naturally lean into a highly expressive, pathos-driven speaking style. If you picture the fast-talking, slightly frantic, emotionally intense energy of someone like Robin from _Stranger Things_, that is my absolute sweet spot. I am incredibly comfortable delivering dialogue that requires a lot of breath, movement, and genuine emotional chaos.

## IV. The Blank Slate (Hire Me!)

I realize that pitching myself as a voice actor without a portfolio of audio samples is completely backwards, but I am putting this out anyway. Sue me. (please don't sue me)

I am incredibly eager to put my skills to use. If you're looking for someone like me, please hit me up. I might not have the demo reel yet, but I promise I will bring exactly the kind of vocal chaos your project needs.
